  <h1>Privacy Policy for 4K Wallpapers</h1>
  <p><strong>Effective date:</strong> July 27, 2026</p>

  <p class="notice"><strong>Before publishing:</strong> replace
    <code>REPLACE_WITH_SUPPORT_EMAIL</code> with the developer support email,
    then host this page at the public URL entered in Google Play Console.</p>

  <h2>Overview</h2>
  <p>4K Wallpapers lets you browse, save, share, and apply bundled wallpapers.
    Wallpaper browsing works offline. This policy explains the limited data
    handled by the app and its advertising provider.</p>

  <h2>Information stored on your device</h2>
  <p>Your favorites, downloaded/viewed wallpaper state, onboarding state, and
    appearance preferences are stored locally on your device. The developer
    does not receive this information. You can remove it by clearing the app's
    storage or uninstalling the app.</p>

  <h2>Advertising and information handled by Google</h2>
  <p>The app uses Google Mobile Ads (AdMob) to show banner and interstitial
    advertisements. The Google Mobile Ads SDK may automatically collect and
    share:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>IP address, which may be used to estimate approximate location;</li>
    <li>app and ad interactions, such as app launches, taps, and video views;</li>
    <li>diagnostic information, such as launch time, hang rate, and energy use;</li>
    <li>device or account identifiers, including the Android advertising ID and
      app set ID where available.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Google uses this information for advertising, analytics, and fraud
    prevention. Data is encrypted in transit. Learn more in
    <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google's Privacy Policy</a>
    and review Google's
    <a href="https://business.safety.google/privacy/">business data
    responsibility information</a>.</p>

  <h2>Your privacy choices</h2>
  <p>Where legally required, the app asks for your advertising privacy choices
    before requesting ads. If a privacy-options entry is required in your
    region, you can reopen it from Settings → Privacy Choices. You can also
    reset or delete your advertising ID in Android's privacy settings.</p>

  <h2>Permissions</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Internet and network state:</strong> load advertisements and
      privacy messages.</li>
    <li><strong>Set wallpaper:</strong> apply an image to the Home screen, Lock
      screen, or both.</li>
    <li><strong>Storage on Android 9 and earlier:</strong> save a wallpaper to
      the gallery after you grant permission.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Children's privacy</h2>
  <p>The app is not directed to children under 13. If you believe a child has
    provided information through the advertising service, contact us so the
    concern can be investigated.</p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>This policy may be updated when app features, SDKs, or legal requirements
    change. The effective date above will be revised when an update is posted.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>For privacy questions, email:
    <a href="mailto:REPLACE_WITH_SUPPORT_EMAIL">REPLACE_WITH_SUPPORT_EMAIL</a>.
  </p>
